WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.190 --> 00:00:07.320
- Good morning ladies and gentlemen.

00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:09.960
On behalf of the President
of Yale University,

00:00:09.960 --> 00:00:11.130
the Commanding Officer

00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:14.040
of Yale Naval Reserve
Officers Training Corps

00:00:14.040 --> 00:00:15.720
and commander of Yale Air Force

00:00:15.720 --> 00:00:17.520
Reserve Officer Training Corps,

00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:20.520
welcome to the Annual President's Review.

00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:23.370
We specifically acknowledge
and thank representatives

00:00:23.370 --> 00:00:25.920
in attendance from Fairfield University,

00:00:25.920 --> 00:00:28.975
Quinnipiac University,
Sacred Heart University,

00:00:28.975 --> 00:00:31.800
Southern Connecticut State University,

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:34.020
Western Connecticut State University,

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:36.330
and the University of New Haven.

00:00:36.330 --> 00:00:39.330
To you and to all distinguished guests

00:00:39.330 --> 00:00:41.673
families, and friends, welcome.

00:00:42.810 --> 00:00:44.340
Today's music is provided

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:47.400
by the United States Navy Band Northeast.

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:50.640
Today's review is conducted
by the midshipmen and cadets

00:00:50.640 --> 00:00:54.213
of Yale Naval and Air Force
Reserve Officer Training Corps.

00:00:56.040 --> 00:00:58.110
Present day reviews have their basis

00:00:58.110 --> 00:01:00.300
in both history and tradition.

00:01:00.300 --> 00:01:03.060
The mass formation of
troops on one long line

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:06.600
at close interval, made possible
the massing of firepower

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.540
from muzzle loaded muskets of yesterday.

00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:13.170
In those early days, the
line of battle was just that,

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:15.390
a line of two or three ranks,

00:01:15.390 --> 00:01:17.460
and looked much like the parade formation

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:21.197
you will see today, the adjuvant
forms the line for battle.

